- Dockerize application
- Create a docker image with the name
- Build a docker image
- Create ECR 
- Create a role for ECR so that we can push or pull images from it
- Login to ECR and push build docker image to ECR
- Create ALB (Application load balancers)
- Create ECS 
- Create ECS task definition (Attach ECS execution permission)
- Create ECS Cluster 
- Create Service inside the ECS cluster 
- Attach ALB to ECS Service
- Access application via ALB public IP address
- Enable Auto Scaling in ECS service to handle traffic spikes automatically.

Security
Use IAM roles (ecsTaskExecutionRole)
Restrict ECR access with AWS IAM policies
Use HTTPS with an SSL certificate (AWS ACM)
🔹 Monitoring
CloudWatch for logs & metrics
AWS X-Ray for tracing requests
Amazon GuardDuty for security threats
